  "raw_meta_yaml": "context:\n  version: \"0.9.0\"\n\npackage:\n  name: herdr\n  version: ${{ version }}\n\nsource:\n  url: https://github.com/ogulcancelik/herdr/archive/refs/tags/v${{ version }}.tar.gz\n  sha256: 1e83bff4b05834ed8281e16f1680e8f3e58375a94b2e3f2b3d021e28e293ef9a\n  patches:\n    # Fix libghostty-vt shared DLL missing ucrt/vcruntime link on Windows (cf. GhosttyLib.zig)\n    # TODO: Submit PR to upstream\n    - ${{ 'libghostty-vt-windows-msvc-crt.patch' if win }}\n\nbuild:\n  number: 0\n  script:\n    interpreter: brush\n    env:\n      CARGO_PROFILE_RELEASE_LTO: fat\n      CARGO_PROFILE_RELEASE_STRIP: symbols\n    content:\n      - if: win\n        then:\n          # workaround for zig 0.15.2 bug: convertPathArg panics on cross-drive paths (Build/Step/Run.zig)\n          - sed -i \"s|assert(!std\\.fs\\.path\\.isAbsolute(child_cwd_rel));|if (std.fs.path.isAbsolute(child_cwd_rel)) return child_cwd_rel;|\" \"${BUILD_PREFIX}/Library/lib/zig/std/Build/Step/Run.zig\"\n      - cargo auditable install --path=. --root=\"${PREFIX}\" --no-track --locked --bins --target-dir=target\n      - cargo-bundle-licenses --format=yaml --output=./THIRDPARTY.yml\n      - |\n        mkdir -p \\\n          \"${PREFIX}/share/bash-completion/completions\" \\\n          \"${PREFIX}/share/zsh/site-functions\" \\\n          \"${PREFIX}/share/fish/vendor_completions.d\" \\\n          \"${PREFIX}/share/elvish/lib\" \\\n          \"${PREFIX}/share/herdr/completions\"\n      - herdr completion bash > \"${PREFIX}/share/bash-completion/completions/herdr\"\n      - herdr completion zsh > \"${PREFIX}/share/zsh/site-functions/_herdr\"\n      - herdr completion fish > \"${PREFIX}/share/fish/vendor_completions.d/herdr.fish\"\n      - herdr completion elvish > \"${PREFIX}/share/elvish/lib/herdr.elv\"\n      - herdr completion powershell > \"${PREFIX}/share/herdr/completions/herdr.ps1\"\n\nrequirements:\n  build:\n    - ${{ compiler('c') }}\n    - ${{ compiler('rust') }}\n    - ${{ stdlib('c') }}\n    - ${{ 'm2-sed' if win }}\n    - brush\n    - cargo-auditable\n    - cargo-bundle-licenses\n    - 'zig >=0.15.2,<0.16'  # upstream issue: https://github.com/ogulcancelik/herdr/issues/285\n\ntests:\n  - package_contents:\n      bin:\n        - herdr\n      files:\n        - share/bash-completion/completions/herdr\n        - share/zsh/site-functions/_herdr\n        - share/fish/vendor_completions.d/herdr.fish\n        - share/elvish/lib/herdr.elv\n        - share/herdr/completions/herdr.ps1\n      strict: true\n  - script:\n      interpreter: brush\n      content:\n        - herdr --version\n        - herdr --help\n        - herdr --skill > /dev/null\n    requirements:\n      run:\n        - brush\n\nabout:\n  homepage: https://herdr.dev\n  documentation: https://herdr.dev/docs\n  repository: https://github.com/ogulcancelik/herdr\n  summary: Agent multiplexer that lives in your terminal\n  license: Apache-2.0\n  license_file:\n    - LICENSE\n    - THIRDPARTY.yml\n    # cannot obtain license by `cargo-bundle-licenses` because of zig libraries\n    - vendor/libghostty-vt/LICENSE\n    # License files for dependencies selected by `emit-lib-vt`.\n    # Herdr enables SIMD:\n    # https://github.com/ogulcancelik/herdr/blob/e16d7d8c07a20f5ee0b4111808680bbcfd7df9ac/build.rs#L49-L69\n    # lib-vt adds uucode and, with SIMD enabled, simdutf and highway:\n    # https://github.com/ghostty-org/ghostty/blob/c5a21edfcbc2d5b46540ad91b7980aca31f5f1f3/src/build/GhosttyZig.zig#L105-L143\n    # https://github.com/ghostty-org/ghostty/blob/c5a21edfcbc2d5b46540ad91b7980aca31f5f1f3/src/build/SharedDeps.zig#L756-L798\n    # Other `.zon` entries, such as vaxis/zigimg, are not linked into lib-vt.\n    # uucode's selected wcwidth extension is informed by the implementations in\n    # resources/wcwidth, so their redistribution notices are included too:\n    # https://github.com/jacobsandlund/uucode/blob/e987cb5d83643bde0945b74d30f530899c64843e/src/x/config_x/wcwidth.zig#L29-L30\n    - licenses/libghostty-vt_THIRDPARTY/\n\n  description: |\n    Run all your coding agents from one terminal, on any box, even over ssh.\n    Each runs in its own real terminal, on a server that keeps it alive when you close the laptop.\n    See blocked, working, and done at a glance, and reattach from your phone.\n\nextra:\n  recipe-maintainers:\n    - eunos-1128\n",
